1
00:00:05,380 --> 00:00:06,940
(Shen Teng)

2
00:00:07,580 --> 00:00:09,540
(Bai Jingting)

3
00:00:09,860 --> 00:00:11,740
(Jia Bing)

4
00:00:12,060 --> 00:00:13,820
(Hu Xianxu)

5
00:00:16,420 --> 00:00:18,300
(Wang Anyu)

6
00:00:18,620 --> 00:00:20,580
(Fan Chengcheng)

7
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:22,820
(Huang Jingyu)

8
00:00:22,940 --> 00:00:24,860
(Wang Churan)

9
00:00:25,580 --> 00:00:32,220
=Natural High S4 (Bonus Episode)=

10
00:00:32,220 --> 00:00:34,000
Guess My Scenario.

11
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:36,860
(Guess My Scenario)
Teams take turns acting and observing.

12
00:00:36,880 --> 00:00:39,560
The acting team takes turns
playing out a scenario.

13
00:00:39,560 --> 00:00:41,520
Three players know the scenario.

14
00:00:41,520 --> 00:00:43,200
One is the blank slate.

15
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:44,560
The observing team must figure out

16
00:00:44,560 --> 00:00:46,160
who the blank slate is.

17
00:00:46,160 --> 00:00:48,280
They get ten questions.

18
00:00:48,280 --> 00:00:50,240
The team that identifies
the most blank slates

19
00:00:50,240 --> 00:00:50,760
wins.

20
00:00:50,860 --> 00:00:52,660
(Teams: Jia Bing's team,
Shen Teng's team)

21
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:53,520
You guys go first.

22
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:54,320
Let's go!

23
00:00:54,320 --> 00:00:54,840
(Let's go)

24
00:00:54,840 --> 00:00:55,960
Did you get that, Anyu?

25
00:00:55,960 --> 00:00:56,560
I got it.

26
00:00:56,560 --> 00:00:58,760
I didn't get any of that. Not a word.

27
00:00:58,760 --> 00:01:00,640
(Totally lost)
You'll get it once you start.

28
00:01:00,640 --> 00:01:01,640
(Round 1, acting team, observing team)
This team needs to close their eyes.

29
00:01:02,640 --> 00:01:03,960
You need to pick a blank slate.

30
00:01:03,960 --> 00:01:04,580
(What do we do?)

31
00:01:04,620 --> 00:01:05,460
(You?)

32
00:01:06,820 --> 00:01:07,700
(I can't)

33
00:01:08,040 --> 00:01:08,400
Who?

34
00:01:09,140 --> 00:01:09,540
Bai.

35
00:01:09,860 --> 00:01:11,420
(Plotting out loud)
Bai.

36
00:01:11,480 --> 00:01:13,140
(Friendly reminder)
We're not wearing headphones!

37
00:01:13,760 --> 00:01:15,960
(Busted)
We only closed our eyes!

38
00:01:16,920 --> 00:01:18,480
Could you not say it out loud?

39
00:01:18,480 --> 00:01:19,620
(Still confused)
Why don't I get it?

40
00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:20,840
I don't get this either.

41
00:01:20,840 --> 00:01:21,840
(Same boat)
Just give it a try.

42
00:01:21,840 --> 00:01:23,560
We'll figure it out.

43
00:01:23,560 --> 00:01:24,040
You got it?

44
00:01:24,520 --> 00:01:25,240
(Then you do it)
I got it.

45
00:01:25,240 --> 00:01:27,360
Okay, blank slate,
hold up one finger at your chest.

46
00:01:27,740 --> 00:01:29,180
(Blank slate: Wang Anyu)

47
00:01:29,640 --> 00:01:30,280
You guys,

48
00:01:30,280 --> 00:01:31,000
take a guess.

49
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:32,440
(Pop quiz)
Who's the blank slate?

50
00:01:32,440 --> 00:01:33,120
Wang Anyu.

51
00:01:33,360 --> 00:01:34,080
Okay.

52
00:01:34,080 --> 00:01:34,440
Come on.

53
00:01:34,440 --> 00:01:35,200
Again.

54
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:35,880
Come on.

55
00:01:38,600 --> 00:01:39,520
I seriously...

56
00:01:39,520 --> 00:01:40,480
Did you get it?

57
00:01:40,480 --> 00:01:41,120
You got it?

58
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:41,840
Yeah, I got it.

59
00:01:41,840 --> 00:01:42,360
I got it.

60
00:01:42,360 --> 00:01:44,260
(Nailed the impression)

61
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:45,520
Hold up one finger at your chest.

62
00:01:49,080 --> 00:01:49,960
Keep our voices down.

63
00:01:50,380 --> 00:01:51,360
(Moving away from the other team)

64
00:01:51,360 --> 00:01:51,960
Bai.

65
00:01:54,840 --> 00:01:55,080
Okay.

66
00:01:55,080 --> 00:01:55,320
Then I'll...

67
00:01:55,320 --> 00:01:56,240
Let's go with Bai.

68
00:01:56,240 --> 00:01:56,720
Okay.

69
00:01:56,720 --> 00:01:57,560
(Still sticking with Anyu)
Fine.

70
00:01:57,560 --> 00:01:59,400
Guys, what if it's Wang Anyu again?

71
00:02:00,700 --> 00:02:02,100
(Bullseye)

72
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:03,340
(It's like he can see everything)

73
00:02:03,420 --> 00:02:05,060
(Plotting again. Me?)

74
00:02:05,100 --> 00:02:05,780
(Bai again?)

75
00:02:06,700 --> 00:02:07,580
(How about Bing?)

76
00:02:08,700 --> 00:02:09,400
(Blank slate: Jia Bing)

77
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:09,720
Let's go!

78
00:02:10,220 --> 00:02:10,820
(Checking the scenario)

79
00:02:10,820 --> 00:02:11,580
(Blank slate: Jia Bing)

80
00:02:11,580 --> 00:02:12,260
(Scenario: You're basketball captains
from four elite schools.)

81
00:02:12,260 --> 00:02:12,940
(You're competing for the only spot
on the provincial team.)

82
00:02:12,940 --> 00:02:13,520
(You all meet in the locker room.)

83
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:14,520
All four of you can open your eyes.

84
00:02:16,120 --> 00:02:16,360
So,

85
00:02:16,360 --> 00:02:17,120
right now,

86
00:02:17,120 --> 00:02:18,680
the three of us...

87
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:19,400
(Throwing them off on purpose)

88
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:20,440
Our scenario is...

89
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:21,900
(We've got the blank slate!)

90
00:02:22,320 --> 00:02:23,560
Bai Jingting's the mole!

91
00:02:25,080 --> 00:02:26,220
What three of us?

92
00:02:26,220 --> 00:02:27,160
(Struck gold)
Bai Jingting! I'm calling it!

93
00:02:27,160 --> 00:02:28,400
Bai Jingting's the blank slate!

94
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:28,960
Call the cops!

95
00:02:28,960 --> 00:02:30,080
What a genius!

96
00:02:30,100 --> 00:02:31,380
(Fooled them)

97
00:02:31,640 --> 00:02:32,520
You sure?

98
00:02:32,520 --> 00:02:34,560
Wanna bet?

99
00:02:34,560 --> 00:02:35,360
You in?

100
00:02:35,360 --> 00:02:35,960
I'm in!

101
00:02:35,960 --> 00:02:37,080
(Betting again, just like that)
How many points?

102
00:02:37,080 --> 00:02:37,560
One point.

103
00:02:37,620 --> 00:02:38,620
(Feeling brave with one point)

104
00:02:38,780 --> 00:02:39,860
(Just one point?)

105
00:02:40,360 --> 00:02:42,520
I bet Anyu could nail this role.

106
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:43,680
He's like this every day.

107
00:02:43,680 --> 00:02:44,880
Actually, this exact scenario

108
00:02:44,880 --> 00:02:46,680
has happened to me before.

109
00:02:47,120 --> 00:02:48,800
(Playing himself)
It really was

110
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:49,880
super competitive.

111
00:02:50,880 --> 00:02:52,960
(Gotta make sure they know he won)
But I still came out on top.

112
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:54,840
So Anyu's still hyped without a mic.

113
00:02:56,080 --> 00:02:56,680
Let's go.

114
00:02:56,680 --> 00:02:57,240
Come on.

115
00:02:57,240 --> 00:02:58,240
Let's pick who goes first.

116
00:02:58,240 --> 00:02:59,360
Number three.

117
00:02:59,360 --> 00:02:59,740
I'm three.

118
00:02:59,740 --> 00:03:00,420
(Acting order: Huang Jingyu,
Wang Anyu, Jia Bing, Bai Jingting)

119
00:03:00,620 --> 00:03:01,620
(The acting begins)

120
00:03:01,620 --> 00:03:02,460
(Scenario: You're basketball captains
from four elite schools.)

121
00:03:02,460 --> 00:03:03,460
(You're competing for the only spot
on the provincial team.)

122
00:03:03,460 --> 00:03:04,640
(You all meet in the locker room.)

123
00:03:04,640 --> 00:03:06,080
How've you guys been playing lately?

124
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:06,520
Not bad.

125
00:03:06,700 --> 00:03:07,900
(Giving it his best shot)

126
00:03:09,120 --> 00:03:09,920
You've been

127
00:03:09,920 --> 00:03:10,840
training pretty well.

128
00:03:10,840 --> 00:03:11,440
You too.

129
00:03:11,840 --> 00:03:13,120
How many points did you score last game?

130
00:03:13,120 --> 00:03:13,800
Didn't you watch?

131
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:14,320
Nope.

132
00:03:14,320 --> 00:03:15,480
Why would I watch your game?

133
00:03:19,220 --> 00:03:20,460
(No warm-up needed)

134
00:03:22,920 --> 00:03:23,800
Wait, that's not...

135
00:03:23,800 --> 00:03:24,860
(That was personal)

136
00:03:26,780 --> 00:03:29,060
(Second actor takes over)

137
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:31,960
See? He's always like this.

138
00:03:33,760 --> 00:03:34,680
You showed up again?

139
00:03:34,680 --> 00:03:35,080
What?

140
00:03:35,920 --> 00:03:36,680
Why can't I?

141
00:03:37,120 --> 00:03:38,600
You weren't that great last time.

142
00:03:38,600 --> 00:03:39,560
I beat you, remember?

143
00:03:39,560 --> 00:03:40,760
I'm the referee now.

144
00:03:41,140 --> 00:03:43,460
(Picking up clues)

145
00:03:43,680 --> 00:03:44,480
Cut me some slack, ref.

146
00:03:45,040 --> 00:03:45,360
Fine.

147
00:03:45,620 --> 00:03:47,220
(Third actor takes over)

148
00:03:47,660 --> 00:03:48,340
(Basketball)

149
00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:49,900
(Copying Anyu's moves)

150
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:51,680
You showed up again?

151
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:52,200
(Basketball)

152
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:53,240
(Copying his lines too)
Why wouldn't I?

153
00:03:55,500 --> 00:03:58,060
(Miming basketball)

154
00:03:58,060 --> 00:04:00,260
(Basketball)

155
00:04:01,020 --> 00:04:01,580
(Basketball)

156
00:04:01,580 --> 00:04:02,940
(Better than you, huh?)

157
00:04:04,660 --> 00:04:05,140
(Basketball)

158
00:04:05,140 --> 00:04:06,660
(Let me show you how it's done)

159
00:04:06,700 --> 00:04:07,700
(Basketball)

160
00:04:08,960 --> 00:04:09,960
You're a loser.

161
00:04:09,960 --> 00:04:10,760
You're no match for me!

162
00:04:10,760 --> 00:04:15,060
(Basketball)

163
00:04:16,920 --> 00:04:18,480
(Now that's impressive)
Which circus is he from?

164
00:04:19,040 --> 00:04:20,240
The pot-balancing act?

165
00:04:20,540 --> 00:04:21,620
(Pot)

166
00:04:23,380 --> 00:04:25,020
(Fourth actor takes over)

167
00:04:25,200 --> 00:04:26,980
Nothing beats
our elite 985 and 211 universities.

168
00:04:26,980 --> 00:04:27,780
(Dropping a major clue)

169
00:04:28,680 --> 00:04:30,640
College basketball teams?

170
00:04:30,640 --> 00:04:31,400
Guess who's the blank slate!

171
00:04:31,780 --> 00:04:32,800
(Observing team reviews
the scenario and asks questions)

172
00:04:32,800 --> 00:04:34,000
I figured that part out.

173
00:04:34,480 --> 00:04:36,360
Anyu's definitely safe.

174
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:38,220
(Analyzing their acting)
Anyu took his shirt off first, right?

175
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:39,480
True.

176
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:40,960
Jingyu was like,

177
00:04:40,960 --> 00:04:42,400
why didn't you watch my basketball game?

178
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:44,400
(Analyzing their lines)
Then Bai mentioned elite schools.

179
00:04:44,400 --> 00:04:45,900
Why was Bing acting like

180
00:04:45,900 --> 00:04:47,500
(Analyzing their roles)
a coach?

181
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:52,000
(Playing it cool)
I was throwing you off.

182
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:53,480
More like you're lost.

183
00:04:55,040 --> 00:04:55,800
Gotta be Bing.

184
00:04:55,800 --> 00:04:56,400
Definitely him.

185
00:04:56,400 --> 00:04:57,400
(Picking Jia Bing)
He played a coach.

186
00:04:57,400 --> 00:04:58,040
Your answer is...

187
00:05:00,560 --> 00:05:01,040
correct.

188
00:05:01,100 --> 00:05:02,300
(Blank slate: Jia Bing)

189
00:05:04,240 --> 00:05:05,400
No, we were too...

190
00:05:05,400 --> 00:05:07,040
(Quick recap)
We gave away

191
00:05:07,040 --> 00:05:07,640
too much.

192
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:09,080
Our clues were too obvious.

193
00:05:09,920 --> 00:05:11,360
Who's "we"?

194
00:05:11,360 --> 00:05:12,280
You!

195
00:05:12,720 --> 00:05:14,360
(No chance of being subtle)
You gave away way too much!

196
00:05:14,360 --> 00:05:15,120
And you...

197
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:17,040
Look who's talking!

198
00:05:17,480 --> 00:05:20,200
(Sharing lessons learned)
We need to clue in the blank slate.

199
00:05:20,200 --> 00:05:21,840
But also show them
who's not the blank slate.

200
00:05:21,840 --> 00:05:22,160
Yeah.

201
00:05:22,880 --> 00:05:23,520
Let's go!

202
00:05:23,520 --> 00:05:25,180
(Round 1, observing team, acting team)
Okay, this team.

203
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:26,960
This side, close your eyes.

204
00:05:26,960 --> 00:05:28,120
Time to pick our mole.

205
00:05:29,060 --> 00:05:29,860
(First choice: Teng)

206
00:05:29,860 --> 00:05:30,540
(Second choice: Chengcheng)

207
00:05:30,660 --> 00:05:31,780
(You do it)

208
00:05:32,100 --> 00:05:32,780
(How about her?)

209
00:05:32,780 --> 00:05:33,700
(Okay)

210
00:05:34,700 --> 00:05:35,940
(Blank slate: Wang Churan)

211
00:05:35,940 --> 00:05:40,380
(Scenario: You're chefs from across China
in a cooking championship.)

212
00:05:40,380 --> 00:05:41,200
(Blank slate: Wang Churan)

213
00:05:41,200 --> 00:05:41,960
Open your eyes.

214
00:05:42,320 --> 00:05:44,240
Let's randomly pick the acting order.

215
00:05:44,480 --> 00:05:44,960
Number two.

216
00:05:45,480 --> 00:05:45,800
Me?

217
00:05:45,800 --> 00:05:46,540
(Acting order: Hu Xianxu, Wang Churan,
Fan Chengcheng, Shen Teng)

218
00:05:46,580 --> 00:05:49,140
(Blank slate goes second)

219
00:05:49,140 --> 00:05:55,020
(Scenario: You're chefs from across
the country in a cooking competition.)

220
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:55,880
We meet again.

221
00:05:56,300 --> 00:05:58,460
(Processing clues)

222
00:05:58,760 --> 00:06:00,160
Seeing you reminds me

223
00:06:01,040 --> 00:06:02,040
of when we were kids.

224
00:06:02,040 --> 00:06:03,680
We trained under the same master.

225
00:06:04,880 --> 00:06:06,220
Cooking's no easy job.

226
00:06:06,220 --> 00:06:06,860
(Dropping a major clue)

227
00:06:06,980 --> 00:06:09,440
(Meet again? Cooking?)

228
00:06:09,440 --> 00:06:10,120
That wok tossing...

229
00:06:10,120 --> 00:06:10,760
I thought it was drums!

230
00:06:10,760 --> 00:06:12,080
I thought he was drumming!

231
00:06:12,080 --> 00:06:12,580
(Great minds think alike)

232
00:06:12,580 --> 00:06:14,340
(Rock star vibes)

233
00:06:16,200 --> 00:06:18,160
If he hadn't said "cooking"...

234
00:06:18,160 --> 00:06:19,180
(Who'd know he was cooking?)

235
00:06:21,720 --> 00:06:22,240
Good luck.

236
00:06:23,240 --> 00:06:25,200
Hope you do well.

237
00:06:25,200 --> 00:06:27,040
Never thought you'd make it this far.

238
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:28,640
(Putting the clues together)
Cooking.

239
00:06:28,640 --> 00:06:30,800
Hope you do well.

240
00:06:30,800 --> 00:06:31,480
Same to you.

241
00:06:31,480 --> 00:06:32,880
Didn't think you'd
make it this far either.

242
00:06:33,720 --> 00:06:34,440
After all these years,

243
00:06:34,440 --> 00:06:35,840
you still haven't improved one bit.

244
00:06:36,220 --> 00:06:37,260
(She must've figured it out by now.
Okay)

245
00:06:38,580 --> 00:06:40,060
(Getting a head start)

246
00:06:40,060 --> 00:06:44,860
(The dish)

247
00:06:44,980 --> 00:06:46,740
(Showing off
his imaginary cooking skills)

248
00:06:48,140 --> 00:06:48,740
(The dish)

249
00:06:49,620 --> 00:06:51,580
(The dish)

250
00:06:51,580 --> 00:06:52,580
(Running out of steam)

251
00:06:53,080 --> 00:06:53,760
Hurry!

252
00:06:53,760 --> 00:06:54,880
Say something!

253
00:06:54,880 --> 00:06:56,000
I can't keep this up! Hurry!

254
00:06:59,400 --> 00:07:00,160
Spicy!

255
00:07:00,160 --> 00:07:01,260
(Spicy)

256
00:07:01,440 --> 00:07:02,400
You still...

257
00:07:03,080 --> 00:07:04,520
look as innocent as ever.

258
00:07:04,900 --> 00:07:07,700
(Innocent)

259
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:10,640
Still the quiet type, huh?

260
00:07:10,640 --> 00:07:13,200
After all these years,
all you can say is "spicy"?

261
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:15,000
Got anything else to say?

262
00:07:15,020 --> 00:07:16,860
(Spicy, spicy, spicy.
Just playing along)

263
00:07:24,600 --> 00:07:25,200
Shandong.

264
00:07:25,840 --> 00:07:26,880
Fan Chengcheng reporting for duty.

265
00:07:28,880 --> 00:07:31,200
Today, I'm making my signature dish.

266
00:07:32,620 --> 00:07:33,620
Braised pork intestines.

267
00:07:35,880 --> 00:07:36,600
For this dish,

268
00:07:37,320 --> 00:07:39,640
I deliberately kept
the intestines' original flavor.

269
00:07:40,140 --> 00:07:41,560
On purpose or by accident?

270
00:07:42,960 --> 00:07:44,280
Teng from Qiqihar.

271
00:07:45,960 --> 00:07:47,000
You're here too?

272
00:07:48,640 --> 00:07:49,320
What'd you make?

273
00:07:50,320 --> 00:07:50,800
Mixed stew.

274
00:07:51,880 --> 00:07:52,720
Some dishes

275
00:07:53,440 --> 00:07:56,760
taste awful.
Don't force people to eat them.

276
00:07:57,940 --> 00:07:58,780
Spicy!

277
00:08:01,440 --> 00:08:02,000
Listen.

278
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:02,760
(Continuing the act)

279
00:08:02,760 --> 00:08:04,440
Not just anyone can come here.

280
00:08:05,200 --> 00:08:06,480
I've sprinkled more salt

281
00:08:06,920 --> 00:08:08,080
than the roads you've walked

282
00:08:08,180 --> 00:08:08,900
are salty.

283
00:08:09,240 --> 00:08:10,480
Salty?

284
00:08:11,940 --> 00:08:13,280
(Tongue-tied)

285
00:08:13,280 --> 00:08:14,320
Of course it's salty!

286
00:08:14,320 --> 00:08:17,560
I've sprinkled more salt
than all the roads you've traveled

287
00:08:17,560 --> 00:08:17,880
combined.

288
00:08:17,880 --> 00:08:18,200
Combined?

289
00:08:18,200 --> 00:08:19,440
Long. I mean, combined.

290
00:08:19,960 --> 00:08:20,280
I'm done.

291
00:08:22,860 --> 00:08:24,180
(Observing team reviews
the scenario and asks questions)

292
00:08:24,200 --> 00:08:25,160
Question for Teng.

293
00:08:27,320 --> 00:08:29,600
(Question 1)
How many contestants are there?

294
00:08:29,600 --> 00:08:30,440
How many contestants?

295
00:08:32,040 --> 00:08:32,880
How would I know?

296
00:08:32,880 --> 00:08:33,920
I'm not the organizer.

297
00:08:33,920 --> 00:08:34,160
I...

298
00:08:35,020 --> 00:08:37,180
(No useful clues)

299
00:08:37,200 --> 00:08:38,080
I think it's Churan.

300
00:08:40,400 --> 00:08:40,920
Churan.

301
00:08:41,680 --> 00:08:44,360
(Question 2)
Why was everyone tossing woks but you?

302
00:08:45,440 --> 00:08:46,460
(Blurting it out)
None of your business!

303
00:08:46,860 --> 00:08:47,480
(Team infighting)

304
00:08:47,480 --> 00:08:48,760
Whose side are you on?

305
00:08:48,820 --> 00:08:50,100
(Just being playful)

306
00:08:52,760 --> 00:08:54,840
"None of your business"?

307
00:08:55,400 --> 00:08:55,960
But why...

308
00:08:55,960 --> 00:08:57,560
(Not letting it go)
Why didn't you toss your wok?

309
00:08:58,160 --> 00:08:59,320
Because...

310
00:09:00,280 --> 00:09:01,280
I did it earlier.

311
00:09:02,040 --> 00:09:03,280
You tossed it earlier or...

312
00:09:03,280 --> 00:09:04,120
Because I'm fast.

313
00:09:04,120 --> 00:09:04,720
You went first?

314
00:09:05,200 --> 00:09:06,160
I already finished.

315
00:09:06,160 --> 00:09:06,760
Finished?

316
00:09:07,800 --> 00:09:08,160
Churan.

317
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:09,320
Churan.

318
00:09:10,240 --> 00:09:10,680
Your answer is...

319
00:09:12,880 --> 00:09:13,280
correct!

320
00:09:15,060 --> 00:09:16,460
(Easy win)

321
00:09:16,600 --> 00:09:18,200
(Blank slate: Wang Churan)
Why? What gave me away?

322
00:09:18,200 --> 00:09:19,240
I didn't toss my wok?

323
00:09:19,240 --> 00:09:20,840
No, when he was acting with you,

324
00:09:20,840 --> 00:09:23,360
what you said
had nothing to do with the scenario.

325
00:09:24,320 --> 00:09:25,000
What was it?

326
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:27,080
Chefs competing
in a cooking championship.

327
00:09:27,640 --> 00:09:28,960
I thought we didn't get along

328
00:09:28,960 --> 00:09:30,440
and suddenly ran into each other.

329
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:32,920
She thought it was a school band.

330
00:09:32,920 --> 00:09:34,520
(So it's my fault?)

331
00:09:34,520 --> 00:09:35,440
You could've just said,

332
00:09:35,440 --> 00:09:37,600
"You're competing too?" That's all!

333
00:09:38,820 --> 00:09:39,940
(Current score: Jia Bing's team 1,
Shen Teng's team 1)

334
00:09:40,020 --> 00:09:40,800
(Round 2)

335
00:09:40,800 --> 00:09:41,380
(Acting team, observing team)
Let's go.

336
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:41,960
Let's go!

337
00:09:41,960 --> 00:09:43,000
Close your eyes, please.

338
00:09:44,340 --> 00:09:45,820
(Volunteering himself)

339
00:09:48,260 --> 00:09:49,900
(Blank slate: Huang Jingyu)

340
00:09:49,900 --> 00:09:52,183
(Scenario: You're leaders
of four martial arts schools)

341
00:09:52,183 --> 00:09:53,720
(at a sword tournament on Mount Hua.)

342
00:09:53,720 --> 00:09:55,480
Okay, open your eyes.

343
00:09:55,480 --> 00:09:56,760
(Blank slate: Huang Jingyu)

344
00:09:56,760 --> 00:09:58,600
Let's pick the order.

345
00:09:58,600 --> 00:09:59,580
Bing goes first.

346
00:09:59,580 --> 00:10:00,500
(Acting order: Jia Bing, Bai Jingting,
Huang Jingyu, Wang Anyu)

347
00:10:05,040 --> 00:10:05,560
Good sir.

348
00:10:07,520 --> 00:10:07,920
What the heck?

349
00:10:08,260 --> 00:10:09,780
(Pretending to be the blank slate)

350
00:10:10,620 --> 00:10:11,660
(What's that supposed to mean?)

351
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:13,520
This year's tournament
is about swordsmanship.

352
00:10:13,520 --> 00:10:14,940
(Pretending to be clueless while feeding
the real blank slate clues)

353
00:10:16,500 --> 00:10:18,020
(Clue received)

354
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:18,760
Forgot my sword.

355
00:10:19,560 --> 00:10:20,520
Go get it, then.

356
00:10:25,960 --> 00:10:26,840
I'll go grab it.

357
00:10:28,720 --> 00:10:30,880
Good sir, here for the tournament too?

358
00:10:31,840 --> 00:10:32,520
Where's your sword?

359
00:10:32,660 --> 00:10:33,620
(Giving him another clue)

360
00:10:36,680 --> 00:10:38,200
Nothing to say to me?

361
00:10:38,380 --> 00:10:39,220
(My turn to talk?)

362
00:10:40,960 --> 00:10:41,400
Seeing you...

363
00:10:41,400 --> 00:10:42,640
I never wanted a fight,

364
00:10:42,640 --> 00:10:44,240
but you left me no choice.

365
00:10:44,720 --> 00:10:45,280
Farewell!

366
00:10:45,280 --> 00:10:45,640
Wait.

367
00:10:45,640 --> 00:10:46,400
Dude,

368
00:10:46,400 --> 00:10:47,520
we barely know each other.

369
00:10:47,520 --> 00:10:49,320
Why're you coming at me like that?

370
00:10:49,320 --> 00:10:50,080
Who's forcing you?

371
00:10:50,300 --> 00:10:51,380
(Give me more clues)
Don't worry about it.

372
00:10:51,720 --> 00:10:52,360
Huang Jingyu.

373
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:55,480
When did I pick a fight with you?

374
00:10:56,120 --> 00:10:57,220
(Out of ideas)
Take care.

375
00:10:57,380 --> 00:11:00,500
(Mind completely blank)

376
00:11:00,640 --> 00:11:01,480
Aren't you a little late?

377
00:11:02,720 --> 00:11:04,000
I just ran into that guy.

378
00:11:04,480 --> 00:11:05,600
Never met him before.

379
00:11:05,600 --> 00:11:06,120
But

380
00:11:06,640 --> 00:11:07,640
he kept saying

381
00:11:09,240 --> 00:11:11,120
he never wanted to fight me,

382
00:11:11,120 --> 00:11:12,840
but I kept pushing him.

383
00:11:12,840 --> 00:11:14,180
(What's that about?)
What'd you do to him?

384
00:11:14,320 --> 00:11:16,040
I didn't do anything.

385
00:11:17,400 --> 00:11:20,420
(Dropping a hint)
Which martial arts school do you represent?

386
00:11:20,880 --> 00:11:22,040
The greatest
of the five sacred mountains.

387
00:11:22,040 --> 00:11:23,520
The greatest
of the five sacred mountains?

388
00:11:25,040 --> 00:11:25,840
Isn't it obvious?

389
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:27,480
Huang Jingyu. I think it's him.

390
00:11:27,960 --> 00:11:29,800
(Prime suspect)
He looked completely lost.

391
00:11:29,800 --> 00:11:31,800
Mr. Huang was like, who's that guy?

392
00:11:31,800 --> 00:11:32,960
That whole...

393
00:11:32,960 --> 00:11:33,960
Who's that guy again?

394
00:11:33,960 --> 00:11:34,720
"Sen jing".
[*Forest police]

395
00:11:34,720 --> 00:11:36,280
Still doing that forest cop bit?

396
00:11:37,120 --> 00:11:38,280
(Question time)
No need to ask.

397
00:11:38,280 --> 00:11:39,500
(Just for show)
Let's ask Bai something.

398
00:11:39,500 --> 00:11:39,860
(Already in retreat)

399
00:11:40,160 --> 00:11:40,760
Go ahead.

400
00:11:40,760 --> 00:11:42,840
At the place you went to today...

401
00:11:42,840 --> 00:11:44,320
(Question 1)

402
00:11:44,320 --> 00:11:45,240
How many people were there?

403
00:11:45,720 --> 00:11:46,360
Was it crowded?

404
00:11:46,920 --> 00:11:48,160
Tons of people.

405
00:11:51,800 --> 00:11:52,760
I wasn't expecting

406
00:11:53,320 --> 00:11:54,480
that question.

407
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:58,520
Neither was I.

408
00:11:58,520 --> 00:12:00,840
Maybe we should plan
our questions next time.

409
00:12:03,500 --> 00:12:04,180
(I'll ask one too)

410
00:12:04,200 --> 00:12:04,760
Bai,

411
00:12:04,760 --> 00:12:07,920
whose side are you on?

412
00:12:07,920 --> 00:12:08,760
(Question 2)

413
00:12:08,760 --> 00:12:11,120
I represent my own school.

414
00:12:12,680 --> 00:12:13,280
It's Jingyu.

415
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:14,880
Mr. Huang.

416
00:12:15,880 --> 00:12:17,000
You asked those two questions

417
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:18,280
and singled me out?

418
00:12:18,540 --> 00:12:19,380
(Trying to stay cool)

419
00:12:20,200 --> 00:12:21,640
Which of these four are you with?

420
00:12:22,280 --> 00:12:22,680
Me?

421
00:12:22,680 --> 00:12:23,920
(Question 3)

422
00:12:23,920 --> 00:12:24,400
You.

423
00:12:24,400 --> 00:12:24,880
You're asking me?

424
00:12:24,880 --> 00:12:25,720
Whose side are you on?

425
00:12:26,320 --> 00:12:27,960
Mr. Huang,

426
00:12:27,960 --> 00:12:29,640
which one are you with?

427
00:12:31,340 --> 00:12:34,260
(Way out of his depth)

428
00:12:34,680 --> 00:12:36,160
Wait, whose side?

429
00:12:36,160 --> 00:12:36,440
Seriously.

430
00:12:37,680 --> 00:12:38,440
We're on the same side?

431
00:12:39,740 --> 00:12:41,540
(Can't bear to watch)

432
00:12:43,940 --> 00:12:45,300
(Still misleading him)
Pretty close.

433
00:12:45,340 --> 00:12:46,580
(Close?)

434
00:12:47,040 --> 00:12:48,400
(Cooking up another trick)
Did you return

435
00:12:48,400 --> 00:12:50,040
(Question 4)
the phone you found to Anyu?

436
00:12:50,040 --> 00:12:50,760
Phone?

437
00:12:50,940 --> 00:12:52,020
(There's a phone too?)

438
00:12:52,090 --> 00:12:53,700
(Messing with Jingyu)
That's a bit too obvious.

439
00:12:53,720 --> 00:12:54,280
Too obvious?

440
00:12:54,720 --> 00:12:56,580
(Completely fooled)
So it's not a period drama?

441
00:12:57,080 --> 00:12:57,640
Hengdian?

442
00:12:59,360 --> 00:12:59,960
No, I didn't.

443
00:12:59,960 --> 00:13:01,200
I took it home.

444
00:13:02,240 --> 00:13:04,160
What was your relationship
with Bai before?

445
00:13:04,160 --> 00:13:04,980
(Question 5)

446
00:13:05,180 --> 00:13:06,180
(I know Bai too?)

447
00:13:06,480 --> 00:13:07,800
Why'd he become a monk? Think.

448
00:13:08,420 --> 00:13:10,300
(There's that much backstory?)

449
00:13:11,640 --> 00:13:13,020
Could I be the reason?

450
00:13:13,020 --> 00:13:14,380
(Imagining a whole drama)

451
00:13:14,520 --> 00:13:16,400
No wonder you wouldn't talk to me.

452
00:13:16,740 --> 00:13:18,540
(Please stop talking)

453
00:13:18,560 --> 00:13:21,160
Before you met Bai today,

454
00:13:21,160 --> 00:13:22,760
(Question 6)
what was the last thing

455
00:13:22,760 --> 00:13:24,040
you did to him?

456
00:13:26,160 --> 00:13:27,560
He went downhill to fetch water.

457
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:30,520
I went uphill to train.

458
00:13:30,520 --> 00:13:31,960
(The story keeps flowing)

459
00:13:31,960 --> 00:13:33,440
I accidentally spilled his water.

460
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:36,240
Maybe that's how I hurt him.

461
00:13:37,120 --> 00:13:37,880
Maybe it's not Jingyu.

462
00:13:38,660 --> 00:13:40,660
(Did I actually fool them?)

463
00:13:40,880 --> 00:13:42,280
He's talking in circles,

464
00:13:42,280 --> 00:13:42,880
but

465
00:13:42,880 --> 00:13:45,120
I think he's on the right track.

466
00:13:45,120 --> 00:13:46,920
He's acting a bit like a mole now.

467
00:13:47,500 --> 00:13:49,580
(They still haven't caught on)

468
00:13:50,080 --> 00:13:51,920
Are all four of them messing with me?

469
00:13:52,780 --> 00:13:54,620
(They know but can't say)

470
00:13:56,560 --> 00:13:59,120
I think it's either Anyu

471
00:13:59,120 --> 00:13:59,680
or Jia Bing.

472
00:13:59,680 --> 00:14:00,400
(Messing with Jingyu)

473
00:14:00,400 --> 00:14:02,480
Then let's vote for Anyu.

474
00:14:03,400 --> 00:14:05,520
Three, two, one.

475
00:14:06,020 --> 00:14:07,140
(Huang Jingyu)

476
00:14:07,400 --> 00:14:07,960
Anyu?

477
00:14:08,600 --> 00:14:09,360
Anyu's out.

478
00:14:10,100 --> 00:14:10,980
(Can't watch anymore)

479
00:14:13,400 --> 00:14:14,600
That round was great.

480
00:14:14,600 --> 00:14:16,840
Messing with the blank slate
is hilarious!

481
00:14:16,840 --> 00:14:18,720
We had him completely confused!

482
00:14:20,660 --> 00:14:21,300
(Round 2)

483
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:22,500
(Observing team, acting team)
Close your eyes.

484
00:14:22,820 --> 00:14:24,380
(Let's pick Teng)

485
00:14:24,980 --> 00:14:27,100
(Blank slate: Shen Teng)

486
00:14:27,100 --> 00:14:31,580
(Scenario: You're exes
of the bride and groom.)

487
00:14:31,580 --> 00:14:34,580
(You all show up at their wedding
and get seated together.)

488
00:14:34,580 --> 00:14:36,300
(So much drama?)

489
00:14:38,760 --> 00:14:40,760
Let's pick the acting order.

490
00:14:40,760 --> 00:14:41,280
Number four.

491
00:14:41,540 --> 00:14:42,980
(Acting order: Fan Chengcheng,
Shen Teng, Hu Xianxu, Wang Churan)

492
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:46,800
(Scenario: You're the bride and groom's exes.)
Wow, this wedding's huge!

493
00:14:46,800 --> 00:14:48,060
(You get seated together at their wedding.)
Let's count the tables.

494
00:14:48,080 --> 00:14:50,240
One, two... ten tables.

495
00:14:50,240 --> 00:14:51,000
At least fifteen.

496
00:14:53,400 --> 00:14:54,200
Where's my name?

497
00:14:54,960 --> 00:14:55,320
Here.

498
00:14:55,320 --> 00:14:55,720
Found it.

499
00:14:58,160 --> 00:14:59,760
These newlyweds...

500
00:15:00,360 --> 00:15:01,600
I can't exactly wish them well.

501
00:15:01,600 --> 00:15:02,440
(Dropping more major clues)

502
00:15:02,440 --> 00:15:03,680
You're Fan Chengcheng, right?

503
00:15:04,240 --> 00:15:05,080
What are you guys doing here?

504
00:15:05,080 --> 00:15:06,000
What are you doing here?

505
00:15:06,480 --> 00:15:08,790
(Shen Teng goes second)
Wait, isn't it my turn?

506
00:15:08,800 --> 00:15:09,040
Yeah.

507
00:15:09,600 --> 00:15:10,560
Used to call me

508
00:15:11,120 --> 00:15:11,920
"baby" every day.

509
00:15:11,920 --> 00:15:13,120
Now she's with someone else.

510
00:15:13,120 --> 00:15:13,680
I just can't...

511
00:15:13,820 --> 00:15:15,140
(Dropping a major clue)

512
00:15:15,420 --> 00:15:16,360
(Clue received)

513
00:15:16,360 --> 00:15:17,880
Back when we were together,

514
00:15:18,400 --> 00:15:19,600
we were way happier than you guys.

515
00:15:22,280 --> 00:15:23,640
Who wouldn't think that?

516
00:15:23,940 --> 00:15:25,900
(Figured it out yet?)

517
00:15:26,120 --> 00:15:27,680
You say you hate her,

518
00:15:28,160 --> 00:15:29,640
but you still came when she invited you,

519
00:15:30,160 --> 00:15:30,600
right?

520
00:15:30,600 --> 00:15:31,600
Still can't let go.

521
00:15:32,480 --> 00:15:33,200
Ever wondered...

522
00:15:33,200 --> 00:15:34,520
(Instantly getting into character)

523
00:15:34,520 --> 00:15:35,920
Which ex you were?

524
00:15:36,440 --> 00:15:37,520
At least one of her first three.

525
00:15:39,300 --> 00:15:40,780
"Qiu"...

526
00:15:40,780 --> 00:15:43,220
"Qianren".
[*A thousand exes]

527
00:15:43,220 --> 00:15:44,620
(This is getting good)

528
00:15:46,680 --> 00:15:47,080
Whatever.

529
00:15:48,240 --> 00:15:49,240
Just eat up.

530
00:15:49,240 --> 00:15:50,760
Get your money's worth
from the wedding gift.

531
00:15:50,940 --> 00:15:52,260
(Blending in perfectly)

532
00:15:53,120 --> 00:15:53,840
Alright.

533
00:15:53,840 --> 00:15:57,200
Let's not talk about this stuff

534
00:15:57,200 --> 00:15:58,200
on such a happy day.

535
00:15:58,200 --> 00:15:58,840
Happy?

536
00:16:02,360 --> 00:16:03,920
Happy?

537
00:16:03,920 --> 00:16:04,680
Well, I...

538
00:16:05,680 --> 00:16:07,000
I wish them happiness.

539
00:16:08,400 --> 00:16:09,360
At least we

540
00:16:09,960 --> 00:16:11,240
once loved each other deeply.

541
00:16:12,400 --> 00:16:13,440
Hi,

542
00:16:13,440 --> 00:16:14,400
I'm just like you guys.

543
00:16:16,600 --> 00:16:18,800
Those two are so cruel!

544
00:16:18,800 --> 00:16:21,120
Seating all their exes together.

545
00:16:21,760 --> 00:16:22,360
Hi.

546
00:16:22,360 --> 00:16:23,360
Why do you look

547
00:16:24,040 --> 00:16:25,040
like you're about to fall apart?

548
00:16:25,880 --> 00:16:27,600
I think I was his first.

549
00:16:28,240 --> 00:16:30,360
Because we actually

550
00:16:30,360 --> 00:16:32,120
met a really long time ago.

551
00:16:32,120 --> 00:16:34,680
I must be his favorite first love.

552
00:16:35,480 --> 00:16:36,280
Look into my eyes.

553
00:16:36,860 --> 00:16:39,220
(Sudden eye movements)

554
00:16:40,580 --> 00:16:42,220
(Time for some eye exercises)

555
00:16:42,480 --> 00:16:43,280
A textbook example!

556
00:16:43,540 --> 00:16:44,980
(A textbook example of eye exercises)

557
00:16:50,360 --> 00:16:51,600
What date did you two get together

558
00:16:51,600 --> 00:16:52,040
back then?

559
00:16:53,800 --> 00:16:55,120
Mr. Thousandth Ex!

560
00:16:56,560 --> 00:16:58,120
Mr. Thousandth Ex!

561
00:17:01,800 --> 00:17:03,320
I've heard all about you.

562
00:17:04,040 --> 00:17:05,040
But seeing you here today

563
00:17:05,040 --> 00:17:06,320
is a real surprise.

564
00:17:06,840 --> 00:17:08,360
Every wedding feast

565
00:17:08,360 --> 00:17:10,640
is worth trying.

566
00:17:10,640 --> 00:17:11,880
Mr. Thousandth Ex here

567
00:17:11,880 --> 00:17:12,920
loves a free meal.

568
00:17:15,080 --> 00:17:16,700
(Question time)
Your answers were all spot-on.

569
00:17:16,920 --> 00:17:17,880
Your acting too.

570
00:17:18,800 --> 00:17:19,200
So

571
00:17:19,200 --> 00:17:21,120
we need some tougher questions.

572
00:17:21,520 --> 00:17:22,840
Let's find some key clues

573
00:17:22,840 --> 00:17:23,320
and ask.

574
00:17:30,140 --> 00:17:31,260
(This isn't a freeze-frame)

575
00:17:31,640 --> 00:17:32,600
Hello? Still there?

576
00:17:32,600 --> 00:17:33,040
You four?

577
00:17:33,260 --> 00:17:35,060
(Thinking. Do not disturb)

578
00:17:37,600 --> 00:17:38,320
Just ask Teng.

579
00:17:39,660 --> 00:17:41,420
(Did I give myself away?)

580
00:17:41,600 --> 00:17:41,880
No.

581
00:17:41,880 --> 00:17:43,520
Teng nailed it at first.

582
00:17:43,520 --> 00:17:44,560
If he didn't know the scenario,

583
00:17:44,560 --> 00:17:45,840
he wouldn't dare act like that.

584
00:17:45,840 --> 00:17:47,120
Since when am I so timid?

585
00:17:50,740 --> 00:17:52,100
(Who are you underestimating?)

586
00:17:52,480 --> 00:17:53,520
I'll ask Churan.

587
00:17:55,160 --> 00:17:57,120
Were there other women at your table?

588
00:17:57,120 --> 00:17:58,400
(Question 1)

589
00:17:58,400 --> 00:17:59,400
I don't know.

590
00:18:03,040 --> 00:18:04,120
Fine, I'll tell you the truth.

591
00:18:04,120 --> 00:18:04,440
Yes.

592
00:18:04,740 --> 00:18:07,220
(Pouncing on the slip-up)
Then why'd you lie?

593
00:18:07,400 --> 00:18:08,480
That was just

594
00:18:08,480 --> 00:18:09,840
my pride talking.

595
00:18:10,520 --> 00:18:12,240
I really want him to admit

596
00:18:12,240 --> 00:18:14,960
I was the one he loved most.

597
00:18:15,280 --> 00:18:16,680
His one and only.

598
00:18:16,680 --> 00:18:17,480
Just pick someone!

599
00:18:17,480 --> 00:18:18,240
Call someone out!

600
00:18:18,240 --> 00:18:19,120
Death's roll call!

601
00:18:19,840 --> 00:18:21,880
Chengcheng started
by mentioning the banquet.

602
00:18:21,880 --> 00:18:23,680
I think he's definitely safe.

603
00:18:23,680 --> 00:18:25,480
Wow, this wedding's huge!

604
00:18:25,480 --> 00:18:26,280
Let's count the tables.

605
00:18:26,760 --> 00:18:27,480
Hu

606
00:18:28,280 --> 00:18:29,280
jumped right in too.

607
00:18:29,280 --> 00:18:30,480
You're Fan Chengcheng, right?

608
00:18:31,800 --> 00:18:33,720
But Churan only spoke

609
00:18:33,720 --> 00:18:34,480
when it was her turn.

610
00:18:35,600 --> 00:18:38,040
Judging by that, I'd say Churan.

611
00:18:39,880 --> 00:18:41,080
Only insecure people

612
00:18:41,080 --> 00:18:42,480
(Pretending to defend herself)
keep fighting for attention.

613
00:18:42,480 --> 00:18:43,280
As for me,

614
00:18:43,280 --> 00:18:44,520
I'm absolutely

615
00:18:44,520 --> 00:18:45,200
confident in myself.

616
00:18:45,720 --> 00:18:47,280
Then let's vote out the confident one.

617
00:18:49,760 --> 00:18:50,480
You sure?

618
00:18:50,580 --> 00:18:51,580
(Don't say I didn't warn you)

619
00:18:51,800 --> 00:18:52,200
We're sure.

620
00:18:52,860 --> 00:18:54,620
(Disguise successful)

621
00:18:54,960 --> 00:18:55,440
Churan.

622
00:18:56,320 --> 00:18:56,920
Your answer is...

623
00:18:57,400 --> 00:18:57,800
wrong.

624
00:19:05,080 --> 00:19:06,640
This one's tough.

625
00:19:07,360 --> 00:19:08,880
My opening was just too good.

626
00:19:09,320 --> 00:19:10,840
You were so good.

627
00:19:10,840 --> 00:19:11,800
I was amazing.

628
00:19:11,800 --> 00:19:13,280
You really nailed the key points.

629
00:19:13,840 --> 00:19:14,560
I think it's Teng.

630
00:19:15,120 --> 00:19:16,680
Teng, you barely spoke.

631
00:19:16,740 --> 00:19:18,020
(Blank slate: Shen Teng)

632
00:19:18,060 --> 00:19:19,300
(Final score: Jia Bing's team 1,
Shen Teng's team 2)
